# Sprite selection (ME-278): Frame Selected frames a sprite's quad (its bounds now count), a click
# on the coin selects it, and a click on its quad's transparent corner goes through: sprites pick
# by their texels, not their whole quad. ED-7: a pick-locked coin can't be clicked.
#   ./.build/Editor_Debug/Havana --scene Assets/Scenes/Tests/SpriteScriptTest.lvl --editor-exec Assets/Scenes/Tests/SpritePickFlows.edscript
wait 30
select Coin
focus-window World View
wait 2
action View.Front
action View.FrameSelected
wait 60
select-none
pick 0.4955 0.5367
wait 10
assert-active Coin
select-none
pick 0.394 0.321
wait 10
assert-selected 0

# Pick lock (ED-7): a locked entity can't be clicked in the World View; unlocked, it can again.
pick-lock Coin | 1
pick 0.4955 0.5367
wait 10
assert-selected 0
pick-lock Coin | 0
pick 0.4955 0.5367
wait 10
assert-active Coin
